.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="A real collider event unfolds in three stages, each with its own physics: a hard 2-to-2 collision fixes the initial parton kinematics from exact relativistic two-body phase space; each outgoing parton then radiates repeatedly (a &quot;shower&quot;) until its energy falls below a hadronization scale, producing a collimated spray of partons -- a jet; and finally every final-state charged particle curves through the detector&#x27;s magnetic field, r = p_T/(qB), while neutral particles fly straight, both depositing their energy once they reach the calorimeter.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/particle/collider_pipeline/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_collision_to_detector_thumb.gif
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/particle/collider_pipeline/plot_collision_to_detector`

